# Flick a Coin's damage is 1, no more (CR 120.3): aimed at Bot2's Ornithopter (0/2) it leaves it alive with 1 damage marked, and
# the rest of the spell happens all the same: a Treasure token under Bot1's control and a card drawn. The Treasure can then pay for
# a mana ability: it is sacrificed for {R} (CR 111.10a, 605.1a).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Flick a Coin
Mountain x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Flick a Coin.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Damage = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token.Activate(Color: Red)
? Bot1.Mana = {R}

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token = (absent)
Bot1.Hand.Count = 7
Bot2.Life = 20
